    {
      "id": "VWeF0hfLDpTPzi8AZ-Kag",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1259.8338389336136,
      "y": -456.8422322972452,
      "width": 578.113018961564,
      "height": 91.24258506337813,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 174895075,
      "version": 131,
      "versionNonce": 2020616626,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788163482574,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* DOS (Difference of Gaussians) + CLAHE (Contrast Limited Adaptive\nHistogram Equalization) is a powerful dual-stage image processing\npipeline primarily used to enhance edge definitions, isolate fine\ndetails, and normalize localized contrast in medical and computer vision\napplications (such as retinal fundus imaging and defect detection)",
      "fontSize": 14.598813610140503,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* DOS (Difference of Gaussians) + CLAHE (Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization) is a powerful dual-stage image processing pipeline primarily used to enhance edge definitions, isolate fine details, and normalize localized contrast in medical and computer vision applications (such as retinal fundus imaging and defect detection)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1EQ1Fbwn8w5IMWj8xWksa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1254.6309443969624,
      "y": -350.8357111452566,
      "width": 570.6672141415922,
      "height": 72.99406805070251,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 937753330,
      "version": 176,
      "versionNonce": 1023992046,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788163477643,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* The Bilateral Filter is an advanced smoothing filter that blurs\nbackground noise while keeping sharp edges perfectly crisp. Standard\nGaussian blurs only look at spatial distance; a bilateral filter looks\nat both distance and pixel intensity differences.",
      "fontSize": 14.598813610140503,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* The Bilateral Filter is an advanced smoothing filter that blurs background noise while keeping sharp edges perfectly crisp. Standard Gaussian blurs only look at spatial distance; a bilateral filter looks at both distance and pixel intensity differences.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fAh005uZbxXpHZylLEMZN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -652.3297989980397,
      "y": -531.9294249113481,
      "width": 580.7403866221805,
      "height": 72.99406805070251,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5i",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1826218606,
      "version": 214,
      "versionNonce": 1580662702,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788163459554,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* HSV Thresholding is a color-based segmentation technique. Unlike the\nRGB color space—where changes in lighting distort the R, G, and B\nchannels simultaneously—the HSV (Hue, Saturation, Value) space separates\npure color (Hue) from its vibrancy and brightness.",
      "fontSize": 14.598813610140503,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* HSV Thresholding is a color-based segmentation technique. Unlike the RGB color space—where changes in lighting distort the R, G, and B channels simultaneously—the HSV (Hue, Saturation, Value) space separates pure color (Hue) from its vibrancy and brightness.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Le7lgErb3R2d1RwLKnra4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -648.4777122553528,
      "y": -349.55775688094786,
      "width": 566.9882400464855,
      "height": 54.7455510380269,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1179306734,
      "version": 190,
      "versionNonce": 123376430,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788163477643,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Fmask is a specialized automated algorithm primarily used in remote\nsensing and satellite imagery (like Landsat and Sentinel data) to\ndetect clouds, cloud shadows, snow, and water.",
      "fontSize": 14.598813610140507,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Fmask is a specialized automated algorithm primarily used in remote sensing and satellite imagery (like Landsat and Sentinel data) to detect clouds, cloud shadows, snow, and water.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uch76mdDuaPcAhJL9smlX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -652.0920840209917,
      "y": -441.1988551580605,
      "width": 571.5430182124788,
      "height": 54.74555103802688,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2010353266,
      "version": 174,
      "versionNonce": 1004807026,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788163482574,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* A Sliding Window is a spatial slicing technique used to scan an image\nby moving a fixed-size bounding box (e.g., 64x64 pixels) across it from\ntop-left to bottom-right.",
      "fontSize": 14.598813610140503,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* A Sliding Window is a spatial slicing technique used to scan an image by moving a fixed-size bounding box (e.g., 64x64 pixels) across it from top-left to bottom-right.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
